UPDATE - Privacy - South Africa (Information officer, PAIA Manual,...) for [~accountid:63622ea17d4645af4f03bd18] [~accountid:617baa2ba989710070897c46] 

*1.) PAIA Manual:* From 1 January 2022 all public and private bodies must have a Promotion of Access to Information Manual (PAIA Manual) in terms of the Promotion of Access to Information Act 2 of 2000 (PAIA). We started to draft a manual [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rxu08CH5WwYDBNs0NoPSZdEt4EDGi5U9/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rxu08CH5WwYDBNs0NoPSZdEt4EDGi5U9/edit|smart-link] . In a next step, we would also have already submitted it to external counsel. Due to several questions (budget, possible hire of a privacy counsel in ZA) the draft was not submitted. 

{color:#ff991f}*A. Proposal: Transmission of the previous draft to Alon and review and possible adjustment. If OC is necessary from his point of view, involvement of OC (Kerubo already has a contact at the beginning of the year).*{color}
{color:#ff5630}*Budget:*{color}{color:#ff991f} *PAIA Manual is committed and only partially touches Privacy. Therefore I would not see the costs necessarily with the DPO team.* {color}

*2.) Information Officer:* Every organization is required to appoint and register an information officer. Information officers are appointed automatically in terms of PAIA. What this means is that every private body (e.g. a company, a trust, or a close corporation) has an information officer by default and no one is exempt. It is the head of the private body (PAIA allows the Information Officer of a private body to authorise any person as an Information Officer)

* To ensure accessibility of a private body, the Information Officer of a multinational entity based outside the Republic must authorise any person within the Republic of South Africa as an Information Officer.
* Each subsidiary of a group of companies must register its Information Officer and Deputy Information Officer(s) with the Regulator.

Kerubo has recommended a person from the public policy team to perform the duties of Information Officer (more like a letter box with internal support). A meeting with the person will took place in February 2022.

{color:#ff991f}*B. Proposal: At the beginning of the year it was discussed that (if there is no legal counsel in South Africa) someone from the Public Policy Team would take over these agendas. Since we now have a privacy counsel (based in South Africa) I would like to ask if there was any discussion during the application process about Alon taking over this role? Please feedback from* {color}[~accountid:63622ea17d4645af4f03bd18]{color:#ff5630} *If so, we would move forward with registration.*{color}


*3.) Reporting duties (PAIA -* _similar to European FoI-frameworks_*):* On 7 May 2023, the Information Regulator (“*the Regulator*”) published a Media Statement notifying Information Officers of public and private bodies of the requirement to submit reports, by *30 June 2023*, regarding access to information requests made in terms of the Promotion of Access to Information Act, 2000 (“*PAIA*”).

The report requires private and public bodies to disclose information relating to their handling and experience of PAIA requests, including information such as:

* the number of PAIA requests received;
* the number of PAIA requests granted (both in full and in part) and rejected;
* the number of internal appeals lodged and the outcomes of such appeals; and
* the number of court applications that were lodged on the grounds that an internal appeal was dismissed.

PAIA requests are *REQUESTS FOR ACCESS TO RECORD (*A record is any recorded information regardless of the from, including, for example, written documents, audio, digital and video materials. A record requested from a public or private body refers to a record that is in that body’s possession regardless of whether that body created the record.) by using a specific form: [https://inforegulator.org.za/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/InfoRegSA-PAIA-Form02-Reg7.pdf|https://inforegulator.org.za/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/InfoRegSA-PAIA-Form02-Reg7.pdf]. Right now we in the DPO team are not aware on any request *(Zero requests)*

{color:#ff991f}*B. Proposal: Clarification with Alon* {color}{color:#bf2600}*(Deadline 30. June 2023)*{color}

