I know you mentioned that Bolt paid for the business rates (despite this also being the landlords responsibility) to avoid any disputes with the local authority. Can you please confirm if any representations have been made by Bolt to the Landlord about paying for the electricity bill? as we need to ensure that we have not implied to the Landlord following previous discussions where Bolt pushed back on these clauses that Bolt would be taking this responsibility. 

I note that the email attached to this ticket dated 24 March 2023 from the lettings manager says the following: 

_“Thank you for your email. I’ve received a response from management and advise that the lease should have stated business rates and electricity are exclusive of the rent and therefore advise that this was our mistake and is not your responsibility. Going forward, I would advise that business rates and electricity will be exclusive and therefore your responsibility”_ 

It is my understanding that as soon as we made the lettings agent aware that this was the landlords responsibility and not Bolts that they then presented Bolt with a new agreement to sign which stipulated that these rates (business rates, gas, water, electricity) were excluded from the rent. I also understand that Bolt prolonged signing this agreement and to-date has not put a signature on this new agreement. Can you please confirm if that is the case? that the new agreement (also attached to the ticket) has not been signed? 

