Investigation so far:

# For some published menus, looker shows more dishes with images than in reality

This case seems to be related to Menu Editor image upload → if the image is too small, we update the params field for the dish with an images field containing an empty transformations array. Since ETL side we just look in storageV1 for an empty images field to decide if the dish has images or not, this case translates to marking the dish in DW as containing images.

In storageV2 we will be looking in the nested transformations array to make this decision (i.e empty transformations array → no images), so it will be resolved in V2. Question is if we need to solve this in V1 as well atm.


{quote}For some other menus, looker data has more dishes than the actual menu has in reality{quote}

Here we found that DW contains dishes that do not exist in live db anymore. This can happen since DW does not replicate delete operations, hence menus which get ingested as drafts and later get updated to active menus, which suffer deletions, will contain such incorrect additional entries. This case will get mitigated in storageV2 as well, since we won’t do physical deletes in menu_item_data in first stage + item data gets referred via the topology field in DB (which only gets updated in time)

{quote}Looker shows less dishes than in reality{quote}

In this case, DA’s queries were counting dishes via stable_ids, which means they were missing the case were 2 dishes with the same stable id are part of different categories. For this case, DA should use stable_context_id to correctly count the dishes

{quote}In some cases, providers disappear from DA’s queries and reappear a few days later{quote}

Looker seems to correctly contain info about provider’s menu, but final used query by DA returns no value. Still under investigation why this happens, does not currently seem to be a data inconsistency issue.

