Hey [~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17], the short answer to your question from the GDPR perspective is no - we cannot disclose any driver’s data to the fleet without the driver's explicit consent, also we cannot change/delete any driver’s data per fleet request without driver's explicit consent. 

Now we are testing the new car payment split feature, in relation to that we are signing new fleet agreements and new authorization forms with drivers who are renting cars from the fleet.

*Under the new authorization form,* drivers authorize Bolt not only to make the payment to the fleet but also to disclose certain data:

# release to the fleet on a weekly basis a file with the following personal details:
- Bolt UUID;
- Name and surname;
- Phone number;
- Transaction details, including reason for the failed transactions.
# upon request, provide access to the fleet to personal details regarding driver’s use of Bolt Services such as:
- revenue earned via the Bolt Platform; 

      - location during the provision of transportation services via the Bolt Platform;
      -invoices issued to the customers on driver’s behalf;
      - driver’s Bolt profile details;
      - statistics of driver trips made via Bolt Platform, including driver score, % of completed trips, acceptance rate, time spent on the Bolt Platform; invoices issued to the driver by Bolt for the use of the Bolt platform.

No other actions are authorized under the above form, thus, no other actions could be taken by Bolt in relation to drivers data without his/her consent. 

*Under the new fleet agreement,* fleets are permitted to upload the list of data of drivers that use  fleet’s car rental services, including UUID and the amount of fleet’s claim to be set off from driver’s revenue. No other actions are permitted. 

BUT for now, the new agreements are signed only with one fleet and its drivers, we hope to sign it also with others, but it will be longer process. 

I am sure that the privacy team and [~accountid:5ecceffac761b10c33d5ba08] are aware of described driver-fleet data processing issue and could provide more information on upcoming solutions 🙂

